        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Vanga</strong></p>",
            "<p>Ancient name of Bengal; mentioned in Mahabharata</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Pundra</strong></p>",
            "<p>North Bengal; ancient kingdom; capital at Pundranagar (Mahasthangarh, Bangladesh)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Suhma &amp; Radha</strong></p>",
            "<p>Parts of ancient Bengal; West Bengal corresponds to these</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Gauda</strong></p>",
            "<p>Medieval name of Bengal; capital at Gaur (Malda district, WB)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Maurya Empire</strong></p>",
            "<p>Bengal was part of Mauryan empire; Chandragupta Maurya</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Gupta Empire</strong></p>",
            "<p>Bengal under Gupta rule; Samudragupta expanded here</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Pala Empire</strong></p>",
            "<p>8th–12th century; Buddhist; originated in Bengal; patronized Nalanda</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Sena Empire</strong></p>",
            "<p>11th–12th century; Hindu; Ballal Sena introduced casteism; Vijayasena ruled</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5huaoxw",
